title: GraphERM
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rath
    given-names: Siddharth
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8584-2877"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rathsidd/GraphERM"
url: "https://github.com/rathsidd/GraphERM"
abstract: >-
  High-performance parallel engine for Euclidean Random Matrix (ERM)
  tracking on graphs. Computes multi-metric eigensystem criticality,
  localized level-spacing contractions, and wavefunction delocalization
  across M = 1000 ensemble realizations. Implements the pyRMT-Sieve
  algorithm across 1D, 2D, and 3D geometric point clouds with uniform
  and periodic grid coordinate regimes.
keywords:
  - random matrix theory
  - Euclidean random matrices
  - Anderson localization
  - GOE
  - eigensystem criticality
  - wavefunction delocalization
  - Shannon entropy
  - computational physics
